title: The Trial of Eugen Leviné
subtitle: Munich's court-martial wants a head.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 6 and crisis = 0 and bavaria_soviet = 1 and bav_power != 2
max-visits: 1

= The Trial of Eugen Leviné

[? if levine_escape = 1 : The false passport was not enough. ?] Leviné was found in a flat in Munich in mid-May and brought before a court-martial for high treason. The prosecutor asks for death. Toller, Mühsam and the others will get prison; the court wants one man to die, and it has chosen the Russian Jew who led the Executive Council.

Leviné does not plead for his life. "We Communists are all dead men on leave," he tells the judges. [? if bav_negotiated = 1 : The truce of 1 May promised courts, not firing squads. The government in Bamberg would rather not break its word in public. ?]

- @campaign: A campaign across Germany to save him.
- @lawyers: Fight it in the courts.
- @martyr: Let him speak, and make the trial a tribune.

@campaign
subtitle: The Left and the Right agree on this: strikes and protests for Leviné.
on-arrival: {!
var chance = 0.25 + (Q.bav_negotiated ? 0.35 : 0) + Q.worker_support / 200;
Q.levine_alive = Math.random() < chance ? 1 : 0;
Q.militancy += 4;
Q.repression += 3;
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 3;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

[? if levine_alive = 1 : Protest strikes in Munich, Berlin and the Ruhr, and an outcry abroad, make the Bavarian government think again. Leviné's sentence is commuted to fifteen years' fortress. ?][? if levine_alive = 0 : The strikes are large, and too late. On 5 June Leviné is shot in the yard of Stadelheim prison, crying "Long live the world revolution!" ?]

@lawyers
subtitle: The Spartacist way: [? if levi_chair = 1 : Levi, a lawyer himself, ?][? if levi_chair = 0 : Levi ?] knows how these courts work.
on-arrival: {!
var chance = 0.15 + (Q.bav_negotiated ? 0.4 : 0);
Q.levine_alive = Math.random() < chance ? 1 : 0;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

[? if levine_alive = 1 : The defence proves that the court-martial had no jurisdiction under the terms of the truce. A higher court sends the case back, and the death sentence is never carried out. ?][? if levine_alive = 0 : The court hears the appeals and rejects them in an afternoon. On 5 June Leviné is shot in the yard of Stadelheim prison, crying "Long live the world revolution!" ?]

@martyr
subtitle: Leviné's own choice. The speech will be read for decades.
on-arrival: levine_alive = 0; worker_support += 3; militancy += 3; offensive_satisfaction += 4; ultraleft_satisfaction += 3; lean_offensive += 1

Leviné's speech to the court is printed illegally in a hundred thousand copies. On 5 June he is shot in the yard of Stadelheim prison, crying "Long live the world revolution!"
